Here is the commit message:
ACCUMULO-4098 Fixed bug with ByteBuffers thats do not start
 at 0

Here is the root cause:
The bug arises from the incorrect handling of `ByteBuffer` instances that do not start at position 0. The original condition only checked if the buffer had an underlying array, which could lead to incorrect calculations of the data offset when the buffer's position and limit did not align with the expected starting point. This could result in reading data from an incorrect position in the array, leading to potential data corruption or unexpected behavior.

Here is the patch:

     public Reader(ByteBuffer buffer) {
-      if (buffer.hasArray()) {
-        offset = buffer.arrayOffset();
+      if (buffer.hasArray() && buffer.array().length == buffer.arrayOffset() + buffer.limit()) {
+        offset = buffer.arrayOffset() + buffer.position();
         data = buffer.array();
       } else {
         data = new byte[buffer.remaining()];
         buffer.get(data);
       }
     }



